<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Fernandez sees no more bank selloffs.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Fernandez sees no more bank selloffs.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine Economy Minister Roque Fernandez denied Monday the government plans to sell the state-run banks Nacion and Provincia de Buenos Aires.</p>
<p>&quot;The only planned privatization is for the National Mortgage Bank.  There are no plans for the Nacion or Provincia de Buenos Aires,&quot; Fernandez told reporters in Washington according to the local state news agency Telam.</p>
<p>The minister spoke after attending a seminar held parallel to the annual meeting of the International Monetary Fund.</p>
<p>The National Mortgage Bank, valued at between $2.0 and $3.0 billion, will be sold in several stages as from June 1997.</p>
<p>-- Carmen Pignotti, Buenos Aires Newsroom 541 318-0657</p>
